When should you use each?
Use merge when:

You want to preserve the actual branching history.
You're working on shared/public branches.
You don't want to rewrite existing commits.

Use rebase when:

You're cleaning up your own feature branch.
You want a linear history before opening a PR.
The commits haven't been shared with other people.

Golden rule: Don't casually rebase commits that other people are already using.